    "created_at": "2019-01-11T15:22:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-01-11T15:22:39Z",
    "body": "I think in these discussions it's probably best not to think too abstractly, since we generally discourage adding many more overloads. Instead it's best to think about its impact on the existing set of APIs on the platform, and making them more reasonable. From that perspective I think making the change is probably a good idea.\r\n\r\nI do agree that, absent a normalization step that removes all trailing `undefined`s, we're not getting fully \"JavaScriptey\" `undefined` treatment.",
